Author: Liz <liz@gewelf.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 30 20:33:51 2026 -0400

    Fix quadratic builder growth, add zero-copy IPC read and faster concat

    Performance (ReleaseFast, Zig 0.17, each benchmark run alone):
    - primitive_builder: 5072 -> 3.8 ns/row. OwnedBuffer.resize grew to the
      exact size on every append, so every builder was O(n^2); it now grows
      geometrically via realloc. Fixed once in buffer.zig for all builders.
    - concatArrayRefs: balanced pairwise merge instead of a left fold, so
      compute take/filter (one piece per index) drop from O(N*k) to O(N log k);
      nullCountForArray uses the SIMD countUnsetBitsInRange.
    - IPC: StreamReader.initZeroCopy slices message bodies out of an in-memory
      source instead of copying (read 34.7 ms -> 2.8 ms in the new
      ipc_roundtrip benchmark); copying reads use OwnedBuffer.initUninit;
      RecordBatch.initPrevalidated skips a second validateLayout for columns
      the IPC reader already validated; setColumnByName uses the schema index.
    - PrimitiveBuilder.reserve / appendSlice bulk fast path.

    Correctness:
    - Builders drop their validity bitmap on finish (array_utils.takeValidity),
      so a reused builder no longer emits an all-ones validity buffer.
    - Slicing a slice of a struct no longer applies the parent offset twice;
      StructArray.field uses the same alignment rule.
    - validateLayout now checks struct children cover the parent window, so
      FFI-imported structs are checked at the trust boundary.

    New benchmark benchmarks/ipc_roundtrip_benchmark.zig (registered in the
    CI benchmark checks and thresholds).

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

